 # Static support boundaries
 
 This project isolates open tool maps, helper-built session instructions, initialization-sensitive subclasses, and ordinary function-tool delegation outside Cloudflare AIChatAgent's supported static relationships.
+
+Static inspection proves `SupportAgent` and its instruction loader, but cannot enumerate the runtime-selected tools spread into its request. It proves only the `StepSupportAgent` runtime class because `prepareStep` can replace that request's instruction. For `DelegatingSupportAgent`, it proves the runtime class, instruction loader, and ordinary `delegate_support` function-tool implementation, registration, and schemas; the implementation's reference to `StepSupportAgent` does not prove a handoff or routing target.
+
+`IndirectSupportAgent`, `UnsupportedOutputAgent`, and `RuntimeInitializedAgent` remain unregistered because indirect generation, array output, and executable fields outside the selected closed class target are not supported static relationships.
+
+Cloudflare runtime and deployment responsibilities are recorded in [the project runtime guide](./runtimes/cloudflare-agents.md).

